on Open Development] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/nine-years-and-a-week-scion-second-edition-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/nine-years-and-a-week-scion-second-edition-open-development/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:41:45-07:00","id":877320,"title":"","content":"cool, so this raise some questions.<br /> <br /> So the separate momentum pools between the GM and players has been axed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T08:35:49-07:00","id":877727,"title":"","content":"Does this alpha slice supersede the spoilers that IanWatson released a while back? because I gotta say, there are a fw changes between Ian's spoilers and this where I prefer Ian's version. For instance, calling the Social control attribute \u201cGrace\u201d rather than \u201cManipulation\u201d, and having an \u201cAim\u201d skill rather than \u201cFirearms\u201d. Though I suppose something like \u201cEloquence\u201d might be better than both \u201cManipulation\u201d <i>and</i> \u201cGrace\u201d, presenting the attribute as primarily being about your competence at communication. <br /> <br /> Of course, I'm <i>also</i> of the opinion that \u201cIntrigue\u201d should actually be \u201cDrama\u201d, and that an effort should be made to expand the scope of the social mode of play to put more emphasis on making friends and inspiring people instead of having the primary focus be on manipulating people. <i>Especially</i> given the nature of Paths in the game (and in <i>Scion</i>, the significance of relationships), presenting the social mode and attributes using terms such as Intrigue and Manipulation puts a bit too much emphasis on the dark underbelly of social interactions for my liking: Intrigue brings to mind playing vicious mind games to gain influence and power, and Manipulation likewise brings to mind social interactions that are geared toward turning others into your pawns \u2014 both of which have a place in the game; but <b>Scion</b> isn't the <b>World of Darkness</b> (nor the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>), and such a cynical view of relationships ought not be presented as the norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T09:25:16-07:00","id":877789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=877320#post877320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the separate momentum pools between the GM and players has been axed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this alpha slice supersede the spoilers that IanWatson released a while back?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There are differences between the two; Scion is a good bit darker than Trinity. Still, I'll think about it some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:57:43-07:00","id":878990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=877789#post877789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. There are differences between the two; Scion is a good bit darker than Trinity. Still, I'll think about it some more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this kinda worries me. Trinity is very dark setting. Good guys nearly always lose there and victories they have are nothing substantial and that is not changing. Every golden age to be turned into dust, One third of the powers are inherently corruptive, one third is given to mankind to enslave them and strip inherent part of what makes them human and the last part is not strongh enough to do anything about it. This is not light setting, It never really was one. How do you go fairly darker, than that in game about heroes of myth? Strip agency and repeat old tales or what ? There is not that much darker to go before you get into pointless grimdark.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T17:19:59-07:00","id":879112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=878990#post878990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this kinda worries me. Trinity is very dark setting. Good guys nearly always lose there and victories they have are nothing substantial and that is not changing. Every golden age to be turned into dust, One third of the powers are inherently corruptive, one third is given to mankind to enslave them and strip inherent part of what makes them human and the last part is not strongh enough to do anything about it. This is not light setting, It never really was one. How do you go fairly darker, than that in game about heroes of myth? Strip agency and repeat old tales or what ? There is not that much darker to go before you get into pointless grimdark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity has patches of darkness (you need them for the drama), but overall every setting has hope and lighter themes. Just looking at 1e, Adventure! was the thrill of action and exploration, and understanding the wonders the world had to offer. Aberrant was the glory of godlike power to change the world, even if that power carried some risk and much temptation. AEon (Trinity) was the expansion of the human experience, realising we're not alone and overcoming obstacles to stamp our place in the universe. <br /> <br /> Yes, each had dark places, but the characters were (by default) working to improve the world. Without darkness to struggle against, the games would lack drama, challenges, and be boring. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean they're dark games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T18:19:59-07:00","id":879144,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Titans have escaped their prison and want to destroy all of creation, and you and a band of Godlings are the only things standing in the path of eternal darkness&quot; sounds pretty darn dark to me. The stakes couldn't be higher, the price of failure more dire - and the rewards of success any greater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T23:09:17-07:00","id":879311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=879144#post879144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Titans have escaped their prison and want to destroy all of creation, and you and a band of Godlings are the only things standing in the path of eternal darkness&quot; sounds pretty darn dark to me. The stakes couldn't be higher, the price of failure more dire - and the rewards of success any greater.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is imo not really darker. What you said is that Scion is more epic. Which is true, but has very little to do with darkness, Assumption, that you can win was hardbaked into Scion. You can overcome these odds and claim vctory. Gods won once. Trinity is opposite. The &quot;good&quot; side never won, they always lost. I feel this is also issue with Bunyip post. Yes all these things were in, but at the end of the day in Trinity base assumption is failure of heroism, yes you can play it differently, but that does not mean it really works as that. and frankly Devs did not really made me belive, that they did changed that, instead of writing equivalent of whistling really loudly and looking away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T01:16:33-07:00","id":879374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=879311#post879311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but at the end of the day in Trinity base assumption is failure of heroism</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wasn't, that's just the way you've chosen to look at it. The default assumption is that humanity has hope and strives to be better. Every age has its setbacks but humans keep improving.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry you don't see it that way, but your posts indicate that you're not at all willing to question whether your assumptions are correct, let alone take an objective view of a new edition with a new system and a broader, brighter setting. I wish you the best of luck in finding the game that you think does conform with what you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T13:53:50-07:00","id":879664,"title":"","content":"What happened to the original Xiutehcutli? He died?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T05:57:00-07:00","id":880094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=879664#post879664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened to the original Xiutehcutli? He died?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Turquoise Lord is known for growing old and becoming young again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T06:57:40-07:00","id":880130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=880094#post880094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Turquoise Lord is known for growing old and becoming young again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the same thing happens To Bernie Sanders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:49:36-07:00","id":890488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/873404-more-storypath-spoilers?p=879311#post879311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is imo not really darker. What you said is that Scion is more epic. Which is true, but has very little to do with darkness, Assumption, that you can win was hardbaked into Scion. You can overcome these odds and claim vctory. Gods won once. Trinity is opposite. The &quot;good&quot; side never won, they always lost. I feel this is also issue with Bunyip post. Yes all these things were in, but at the end of the day in Trinity base assumption is failure of heroism, yes you can play it differently, but that does not mean it really works as that. and frankly Devs did not really made me belive, that they did changed that, instead of writing equivalent of whistling really loudly and looking away.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Aeon specifically was all about what humanity is capable of accomplishing if only it can work together. The only game out of the original three with a pessimistic outlook was Aberrant, to the point that the original Aeon developer felt it was a thematic misstep IIRC (you can see clearly how Aberrant's libertarian ethos and mistrust of groupefforts and &quot;Utopianism&quot; clashes with Aeon's New Deal ethos).<br /> <br /> Trinity Continuum is all about people being able to change the world for the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-14-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}